# Azure RBAC Lab – Week 1 (Identity & Basics)

This project demonstrates basic Azure identity and access management concepts as part of my **AZ‑104 study journey**.

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Create users and groups in Azure Active Directory.
- Assign Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) roles to manage permissions.
- Organize resources using subscriptions and resource groups.

---

## 🛠️ Scripts

### 1. Create a User
```bash
az ad user create \
  --display-name "LabUser1" \
  --user-principal-name labuser1@yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com \
  --password "StrongP@ssword123!"


###2. Create a Group

az ad group create \
  --display-name "LabAdmins" \
  --mail-nickname "labadmins"


3. Assign RBAC Role

az role assignment create \
  --assignee labuser1@yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com \
  --role "Contributor" \
  --scope /subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<resource-group-name>


Notes
Azure AD is the identity service for Azure resources.

RBAC ensures least privilege by assigning roles at different scopes (subscription, resource group, resource).

Resource Groups help organize resources logically for management and billing

Reflection
This week I learned how RBAC enforces security boundaries in Azure. Creating users, groups, and assigning roles gave me hands‑on experience with identity management.
